      "description": "Watch KSK Beveren vs OH Leuven highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 7, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League delivered a high-stakes encounter between KSK Beveren and Lommel United , with tactical discipline taking center stage from the first whistle. Both sides looked to establish early control in a match that promised to be decided by the narrowest of margins. Drama Before the Interval The match, held on September 7, 2026 , began with both teams testing each other's defensive resilience. The first significant moment of friction occurred in the 36th minute when Han-Beom Lee was shown a yellow card for a mistimed challenge. As the first half drew to a close, disaster struck for the visitors. In the 45th minute, Timothy Eyoma inadvertently diverted the ball into his own net, handing KSK Beveren a crucial lead just seconds before the referee blew for half-time. Second Half Tension and Tactical Shifts The second period started with Lommel United pushing for an equalizer, but their frustrations grew as Juho Talvitie received a yellow card in the 47th minute. The flow of the game became increasingly fragmented as both managers turned to their benches. Mamadou Diakhon made way for Jan Virgili at the hour mark, followed shortly by Sam De Grand replacing Shawn Adewoye . These changes aimed to inject fresh energy, but the KSK Beveren defense remained organized under pressure. Closing Stages and Final Whistle As the clock ticked toward the conclusion, the physical nature of the game intensified, leading to a booking for Freddie Potts in the 82nd minute. A flurry of late substitutions saw the likes of Felix Lemarechal , Hugo Siquet , and Andrej Vasovic enter the fray. Despite Lommel United's desperate attempts to find a way back into the game during the five minutes of stoppage time, the hosts held firm to secure the victory following a tense and hard-fought battle."
